From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: 导出 saved_command_line 供 qca-nss-dp 读取 mem-profile=

qca-nss-dp 在初始化时读取内核命令行，以支持 QSDK 的 "mem-profile="
启动参数（决定 EDMA 环形缓冲区大小与 NSS_DP_MEM_PROFILE_* 标志）：

  nss_dp_main.c:45:  extern char *saved_command_line;
  nss_dp_main.c:232: flags = __get_mem_profile_flag(saved_command_line);

QSDK 内核在 init/main.c 里导出该符号，主线 6.12 不导出，modpost 因此失败：

  ERROR: modpost: "saved_command_line" [qca-nss-dp.ko] undefined!

本补丁在 qualcommbe 的 6.12 patch 目录中新增 0144，为 init/main.c 增加
EXPORT_SYMBOL(saved_command_line)。导出不改变行为：该指针是
__ro_after_init，驱动只在初始化时读一次。备选方案是放弃 mem-profile 检测、
固定使用 HIGH profile，但那会从移植里去掉一个已文档化的 QSDK 启动参数。

分类：必须 shim（厂商内核 ABI；符号在主线存在但未导出）。

diff -ruN a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0144-init-export-saved-command-line.patch b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0144-init-export-saved-command-line.patch
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0144-init-export-saved-command-line.patch
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0144-init-export-saved-command-line.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+init: export saved_command_line for qca-nss-dp
+
+qca-nss-dp reads the kernel command line to honour the QSDK
+"mem-profile=" boot argument, which selects the EDMA ring sizes and the
+NSS_DP_MEM_PROFILE_* flag used across the data plane:
+
+  nss_dp_main.c:45:  extern char *saved_command_line;
+  nss_dp_main.c:232: flags = __get_mem_profile_flag(saved_command_line);
+
+QSDK's kernel exports the symbol, mainline 6.12 does not, so modpost
+fails the link with:
+
+  ERROR: modpost: "saved_command_line" [qca-nss-dp.ko] undefined!
+
+Exporting it changes no behaviour: the pointer is __ro_after_init and the
+driver only reads it once at init.  The alternative would be to drop
+mem-profile detection and hard-code the HIGH profile, which would remove
+a documented QSDK boot parameter from the port.
+
+Classification: must-shim (vendor kernel ABI); the symbol exists in
+mainline but is not exported.
+
+---
+--- a/init/main.c
++++ b/init/main.c
+@@ -142,6 +142,7 @@
+ /* Untouched saved command line (eg. for /proc) */
+ char *saved_command_line __ro_after_init;
+ unsigned int saved_command_line_len __ro_after_init;
++EXPORT_SYMBOL(saved_command_line);
+ /* Command line for parameter parsing */
+ static char *static_command_line;
+ /* Untouched extra command line */
